WEBVTT

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.840
It doesn't really suit me...

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.540
Maybe I should have gone to a private school...

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:01.470
Thank you very much.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.110
Jellyfish.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:37.220
It wasn't like this jellyfish, was it?

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:40.140
Was it?

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:42.510
Because it could live outside the water, right?

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:45.150
Right?

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.190
Grownups just don't get it...

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:50.120
Get it.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.970
Jellyfish... the thing that lives in the sea?

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.700
Ah, I'll be late for soccer practice.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.640
Shut up! Go away!

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:29.210
Diablomon Strikes Back

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.780
Gotta hurry, gotta hurry...

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.760
"Computer room is closed for maintenance."

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:40.390
Digi Digi?

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:41.580
Mon Mon.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.740
Excuse me...

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:47.950
That makes all of us.

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:54.000
Where are Mimi-san, Jou-san and Sora-san?

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.530
Mimi-san is on her flight here from America.

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:04.740
Like I said, don't you have natto beans? Please!

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:08.520
Jou-san is registering for high school.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.920
No, I'm sure I passed it!

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.170
Where's Sora-san?

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.090
On the tennis club trip.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:21.340
She's on her way here now.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:24.010
So, what's going on?

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.430
Please take a look at this.

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:30.390
Who's that guy?

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:33.060
Sorry... but it's me.

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:37.400
These are spreading all over the Net.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:43.360
What a stupid prank!

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:46.740
It's all Diablomon's doing.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.010
Diablomon?

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:50.860
The one who appeared in the Net three years ago?

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:53.880
Didn't Omegamon defeat him?

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.790
We thought he did...

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:58.210
But he survived.

00:03:58.570 --> 00:03:59.920
How is that possible?

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:03.840
His data must have survived the battle and multiplied.

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:09.020
Now he's sending Kuramon to the Real World through e-mail.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:10.220
To the Real World?

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:14.980
If you open this mail, this strange jellyfish-like creature comes out.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:18.150
I-Is that safe?

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:21.860
Yeah... this is just a capture.

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:27.560
He even tried to launch nuclear missiles.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:31.250
Who knows what he would do if he got to the Real World!

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:36.160
Koshiro, can you open a gate to the Net?

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.460
There must be a source the Kuramon are coming from, somewhere.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:41.550
We'll strike there!

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:43.680
I'm going too!

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:48.600
Daisuke, we're leaving the Kuramon to you.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:52.580
It'd be a problem if they evolved in this world.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:57.330
Yes, leave the rest to Omegamon.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:03.730
Taichi-san and Yamato-san, head to the Net gateway and join Agumon and Gabumon,

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:06.610
and then I'll direct you to the source of the mails.

00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:12.040
They'll be all right, Hikari.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.500
Huh?

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.960
Ishida Yamato, 980 yen.

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:21.180
Yagami Taichi, 380 yen.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:26.110
Everyone else, capture the Kuramon.

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:28.800
Try not to attack them so they don't evolve.

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:34.690
Use your D-3 to open the gate and send the captured Kuramon here.

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:38.650
I'll ask Gennai-san what to do with them for now.

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:44.400
Okay, we got one!

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:48.070
Here it is...

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:49.820
There we go.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:52.340
No! It's mine!

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:55.790
Um, that's dangerous, so let it go already...

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:00.130
'kay?

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:01.190
You're a good girl, right?

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:02.250
So listen to us!

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:05.490
But you have them too!

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:06.440
W-Well...

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:07.970
They're just, y'know...

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:11.910
Daisuke-kun, please head to Shibuya next.

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:17.140
I shouldn't have borrowed my sister's phone...

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:40.750
<i>Don't release your pets here, please.</i>

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.560
That's not a pet!

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:47.760
We're sending you a Kuramon.

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:47.760
Takeru

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.960
You can send them while they're Kuramon,

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:53.400
but their data would take up too much space if they evolved, so you wouldn't be able to.

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:59.040
Koshiro-han, there are still a lot of those Kuramon heading over there!

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:02.710
Taichi-san and the rest are already in the Net.

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:07.730
But the Kuramon's target should be Omegamon...

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:09.400
Then, why...?

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:16.530
Just how many of them do we have to catch?

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:24.190
Hey, Ken.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:25.960
What?

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:26.710
Turn that off!

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:32.430
Wh-What the hell is this!?

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:36.140
Don't use your cellphones here!

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:40.060
Why are the Kuramon still appearing?

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.560
I told you not to evolve!

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:43.720
But...

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.490
And then you go and attack them!

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:46.740
But...

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:49.000
Well, at least we captured them all.

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.610
Koshiro-san will get mad at us...

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:56.950
You attacked a Kuramon?

00:07:56.950 --> 00:08:00.090
<i>Yeah... but it didn't evolve.</i>

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:01.460
Didn't evolve?

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:03.290
Why?

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:07.250
Koshiro-han! Taichi-han and the others are almost at the source point!

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:14.850
Agumon, be careful!

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:16.510
Ah, damn it...

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:19.680
Why are those things ignoring us?

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:21.960
We're leaving that to Daisuke and the rest.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.310
We just have to defeat the big one.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:25.060
Right.

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:28.400
Let's go!

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:12.780
Let's chase after it!

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:15.290
Daisuke! Look!

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:19.530
What's going on here?

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:34.630
Damn it... attack Diablomon, the source!

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:49.730
No!

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:52.500
Koshiro-han, message from Takeru-han and Hikari-han:

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:55.450
They're heading to help Taichi-han's group!

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:59.860
Understood. Please tell them to be very careful.

00:10:00.610 --> 00:10:03.330
Diablomon is planning something.

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:06.870
Takeru-san, be careful.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.760
We're counting on you.

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:11.250
Sure. Leave those Kuramon to me!

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:15.350
Big brother...

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:18.390
It'll be fine.

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:19.720
We can still make it.

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:22.450
Let's hurry.

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:26.640
Be very careful, okay?

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:30.100
No way...

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:33.040
Someone sent it to me again.

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:33.840
Huh?

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:38.530
I couldn't see this fight back then because I didn't have a PC at home.

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.350
Is that the mail thing?

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:40.990
Yep!

00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:44.580
Can't he go faster?

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.490
Use a better attack!

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.960
Now of all times...

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.680
Hello?

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:57.630
<i>Daisuke-kun, Hikari-san and Takeru-kun are heading towards Omegamon's location.</i>

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:00.340
<i>You guys take care of the Kuramon.</i>

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:03.540
Hikari-chan!

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:06.720
Hold it, we should follow Koshiro-san's directions.

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:09.770
What, and leave them alone?

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:10.930
Daisuke!

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:12.890
Look at that!

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:26.910
Big brother!

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:35.590
Brother!

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:37.380
Takeru!

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:38.000
Hikari!

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:43.510
Excuse me!

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:45.510
Let me borrow that, please!

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:48.520
Daisuke, what are you doing?

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:50.430
We're going there too.

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:54.180
We're going to save Hikari-chan and everyone!

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.590
Please, let me borrow it!

00:12:00.270 --> 00:12:00.900
Here.

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:05.800
<i>Miyako? Guide us through the Net!</i>

00:12:29.170 --> 00:12:31.380
Bingo!

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:33.390
All right!

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:34.570
Miyako-san!

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:37.810
Though... did I open too many gates?

00:12:38.370 --> 00:12:39.400
Angewomon!

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:41.530
Right! Omegamon!

00:12:49.570 --> 00:12:50.660
Big brother!

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:51.580
Got it!

00:12:58.650 --> 00:12:59.380
Brother!

00:12:59.380 --> 00:12:59.960
Yeah!

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:26.360
The gates...

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:27.790
...are closing.

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:34.500
What's going on?

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:37.700
Don't worry, Hikari.

00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:39.710
Leave this to me.

00:13:55.820 --> 00:13:56.430
What?

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:01.980
So it <i>was</i> a trap!

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:07.530
How did this happen...?

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:11.380
Don't mess with me!

00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:13.950
Daisuke! We've gotta do something about them!

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:14.910
Right!

00:14:15.260 --> 00:14:16.870
Eh? What?

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:20.500
Okay, I'll contact Iori then. Yeah, at Odaiba.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:24.000
All right, Miyako-sama will show you all what she's capable of!

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:27.300
"To the Kuramon:"

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.340
"We'll be waiting"

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:31.260
"at Tokyo Bay."

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:33.890
"The Chosen Children."

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:41.960
Why at Tokyo Bay?

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:44.010
We can't fight them in the middle of the city!

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:46.870
If we ride on Imperialdramon, we can quickly...

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:49.400
Daisuke!

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:50.570
Ken-chan!

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:51.930
V-mon...

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:52.700
Wormmon...

00:14:53.480 --> 00:14:56.730
<i>Train service is temporarily on hold.</i>

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:02.710
Hi there!

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:06.840
It's you, Mimi-san...

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:08.930
What's that?

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:12.340
At least say "Welcome back!"

00:15:15.050 --> 00:15:17.220
Um... it's not the time for that.

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.330
Where are we going?

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:34.370
No idea...

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:37.940
Still, Diablomon is a frightening being.

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:42.150
Thinking he might be defeated, he sent all those Kuramon here.

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:43.330
What do you mean?

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:47.480
It would be difficult for Diablomon to come to our world in that form,

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:51.800
but his Baby form Kuramon has a much lower amount of data.

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:58.520
This way he made sure that even if we defeat him, the Kuramon will take his place.

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:03.730
When Miyako-kun opened the gates, that allowed many more Kuramon to live.

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:07.570
And with that amount of Kuramon in the Real World...

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:11.030
...we can't get rid of them all.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:14.820
<i>The JR lines are now operational.</i>

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:26.670
Yeah, see you at Rainbow Bridge.

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:29.090
Going to Rainbow Bridge

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:29.090
I'm bringing snacks!

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:33.720
A taxi won't do...

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:35.220
We'll have to run there.

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:37.930
Miyako, how are things at Tokyo Bay?

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:38.610
Well...

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:40.010
Miyako-san!

00:16:40.010 --> 00:16:41.490
Iori!

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:44.350
Yeah, I met up with Iori, but this is getting serious!

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:52.280
It's a sea of Kuramon! Get over here now!

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:53.370
<i>Got it.</i>

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:54.000
Miyako-san!

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:58.830
<i>Hey, what's wrong, Miyako?</i>

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:00.530
<i>Miyako? Answer me!</i>

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:01.910
They're starting to evolve...

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:08.260
Into... Diablomon?

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:09.090
No...

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:13.130
A DigiEgg...

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:16.470
What's going... to be born?

00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:19.600
Hey, Koshiro-kun...

00:17:22.460 --> 00:17:25.020
Anyway, we have to get there before the DigiEgg hatches!

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:27.250
So, where are we?

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:29.810
Still in Shibuya!

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:35.000
Let's hurry!

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.240
Are we gonna make it in time?

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:53.500
It's hatching...

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:08.520
W-Wow!

00:18:14.270 --> 00:18:15.920
What a huge amount of data...

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:17.240
Can't we do anything?

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:19.740
There's too much data.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:22.200
We can't send him back to the Net like this!

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:38.270
We're back.

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:46.040
Hello?

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:48.930
<i>Daisuke, this is bad! The DigiEgg hatched!</i>

00:18:48.930 --> 00:18:50.580
<i>But Taichi-san and the rest are here too so...</i>

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:52.560
Okay! We'll hurry up!

00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:56.940
This... is kinda tough...

00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:01.230
You can't take the ball from me like that.

00:19:01.230 --> 00:19:02.740
Shut it!

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:44.160
Come on, you can't even call it a fight!

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:48.150
Daisuke, hurry up...

00:19:48.150 --> 00:19:48.910
Ken-chan...

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:52.420
Are we... going to make it?

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:58.630
Don't you always get some stupidly big power when things are going really badly?

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:03.130
Daisuke-kun!

00:20:06.510 --> 00:20:07.760
Senpai...

00:20:11.260 --> 00:20:14.050
Koshiro told me you were coming this way!

00:20:14.050 --> 00:20:15.940
Use this!

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:19.160
Senpai, we're two guys.

00:20:22.180 --> 00:20:23.570
Coming through!

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:27.330
Wait, please!

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:28.990
Wh-What? What is it?

00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:57.950
N-No...

00:20:57.950 --> 00:20:58.940
Omegamon...

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:10.120
Omegamon!

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:17.890
Omegamon...

00:21:17.890 --> 00:21:18.960
No!

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:24.350
Koshiro-han, pull yourself together!

00:21:38.530 --> 00:21:40.440
Omegamon...

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:44.110
Daisuke!

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:45.150
Ken-chan!

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:47.310
V-mon?

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:47.310
Wormmon?

00:21:53.720 --> 00:21:55.960
Move out of the way!

00:21:56.730 --> 00:21:58.930
I said move!

00:21:58.930 --> 00:22:00.380
Excuse me!

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:08.660
V-mon!!

00:22:03.240 --> 00:22:08.660
Wormmon!!

00:22:22.760 --> 00:22:23.860
Everyone...

00:22:24.410 --> 00:22:25.900
Go!

00:22:30.360 --> 00:22:31.660
V-mon, sorry I took so long!

00:22:31.660 --> 00:22:33.410
Let's do it, Wormmon!

00:22:34.550 --> 00:22:35.830
Yeah!

00:22:37.730 --> 00:22:39.360
V-mon, evolve!

00:22:39.370 --> 00:22:44.980
full speed de mawari hajimeta story

00:22:39.370 --> 00:22:44.980
At full-speed, a story starts spinning

00:22:40.090 --> 00:22:42.020
XV-mon!

00:22:42.020 --> 00:22:44.460
Wormmon, evolve!

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:46.630
Stingmon!

00:22:44.980 --> 00:22:49.080
akaku daichi someageru

00:22:44.980 --> 00:22:49.080
painting the earth red

00:22:46.630 --> 00:22:49.110
Jogress-evolve!

00:22:49.110 --> 00:22:51.220
Paildramon!

00:22:50.920 --> 00:22:56.890
chikyuu-gi ni wa garandou ni natta paradise

00:22:50.920 --> 00:22:56.890
The globe is but an empty paradise

00:22:51.220 --> 00:22:53.790
Ultimate-evolve!

00:22:54.350 --> 00:22:56.890
Imperialdramon!

00:22:56.890 --> 00:23:01.270
boku-ra no te de sukuidasou

00:22:56.890 --> 00:23:01.270
Let's free it by ourselves

00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:08.320
hateshinaku tsuzuku sakamichi o

00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:08.320
Now put all your heart into running

00:23:07.280 --> 00:23:09.320
Hang in there!

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:13.810
ima omoikiri kakenukete far away

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:13.810
through the steep endless road, far away

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:23.330
tachiagare! yuusha wa boku no naka ni iru

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:23.330
I gotta stand up! There's a hero in me

00:23:23.330 --> 00:23:28.960
sobietatsu target makeru wake ni wa ikanai

00:23:23.330 --> 00:23:28.960
I'll never lose to such a towering target

00:23:24.050 --> 00:23:25.460
Looks like I'm late.

00:23:25.460 --> 00:23:26.720
Sora!

00:23:26.720 --> 00:23:28.960
Taichi! Yamato!

00:23:28.960 --> 00:23:35.090
moeagare! kodou wa mune o kogashiteru

00:23:28.960 --> 00:23:35.090
I gotta flare up! The heartbeat in my chest

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:35.890
Not Imperialdramon too...

00:23:35.090 --> 00:23:41.660
wasurerareta ashita torimodoshi ni ikun da

00:23:35.090 --> 00:23:41.660
I'll take back our forgotten tomorrow

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:36.650
Dammit!

00:23:36.650 --> 00:23:37.680
We won't lose!

00:23:41.660 --> 00:23:47.440
atsui battle okose

00:23:41.660 --> 00:23:47.440
Starting a hot battle!

00:24:11.630 --> 00:24:13.970
N-No way... it didn't work?

00:24:22.720 --> 00:24:24.550
We're done for...

00:24:24.550 --> 00:24:26.310
We can't defeat him.

00:24:26.310 --> 00:24:27.440
Don't give up.

00:24:28.040 --> 00:24:32.340
We always fight with all we have until the end, right?

00:24:41.590 --> 00:24:46.250
That's right... you never give up until the very end.

00:24:46.250 --> 00:24:50.000
We believe in you all!

00:24:52.470 --> 00:24:54.000
A Holy Ring?

00:24:54.000 --> 00:24:56.800
Yeah... filled with everyone's hope.

00:25:08.520 --> 00:25:10.480
Take it!!

00:25:10.480 --> 00:25:12.280
It's everyone's power!

00:25:16.510 --> 00:25:17.930
This is...

00:25:17.930 --> 00:25:18.990
Everyone's...

00:25:32.800 --> 00:25:35.800
Go!

00:25:47.970 --> 00:25:49.100
Kuramon?

00:25:49.100 --> 00:25:52.900
His data will survive like this.

00:25:53.860 --> 00:25:55.450
The trash can?

00:25:56.980 --> 00:26:00.370
The Kuramon can be sent back with everyone's cellphones!

00:26:00.370 --> 00:26:01.580
Bingo!

00:26:43.540 --> 00:26:46.540
Everyone, aim the light at the sword!

00:26:53.620 --> 00:26:57.170
Concentrate it on the sword!

00:27:38.300 --> 00:27:42.410
Using everyone's cellphones to absorb their data...

00:27:38.340 --> 00:27:42.380
Izumi-senpai, I'm sending you

00:27:38.340 --> 00:27:42.380
the Kuramon.

00:27:38.340 --> 00:27:42.380
We leave them to you. (^_^) v

00:27:38.340 --> 00:27:42.380
Miyako

00:27:42.410 --> 00:27:44.690
Great idea, Iori-kun.

00:27:44.690 --> 00:27:48.220
Argh! How do you turn this off!?

00:28:19.360 --> 00:28:21.190
I'm tired...

00:28:31.100 --> 00:28:41.760
nee haru no tobira mukougawa ni wa donna ashita ga hirogatteru no?

00:28:31.100 --> 00:28:41.760
What kind of future is growing beyond autumn's door?

00:28:42.450 --> 00:28:52.890
nee nazeka saikin toki no nagare ga kyuu ni hayakute tomadotteru yo

00:28:42.450 --> 00:28:52.890
It's strange how time has been flowing faster lately

00:28:52.890 --> 00:29:04.800
namae de yobiatta toki tanoshii koto ga ugokidasu ki ga shita

00:28:52.890 --> 00:29:04.800
I knew fun things would happen when we called each other's name

00:29:04.800 --> 00:29:16.450
itsuka wa natsukashiku naru nante kigatsukazu ni ita yo

00:29:04.800 --> 00:29:16.450
I've just realized that we'll look back on these memories someday

00:29:16.450 --> 00:29:22.090
itsu mademo wasurenai onaji mado kara mita

00:29:16.450 --> 00:29:22.090
I'll never forget looking out of the same window

00:29:22.090 --> 00:29:27.750
sakura no ki semi no koe itsumo soba ni ita yo ne

00:29:22.090 --> 00:29:27.750
The cherry trees, the sound of cicadas, they were always nearby

00:29:27.750 --> 00:29:34.470
waratteta naite ita issho ni sugoshita hibi

00:29:27.750 --> 00:29:34.470
We laughed, we cried, and I'll keep

00:29:34.470 --> 00:29:39.170
kono mune no naka arukidaseru

00:29:34.470 --> 00:29:39.170
our days together in my heart

00:29:39.170 --> 00:29:42.060
soba ni itemo friend...

00:29:39.170 --> 00:29:42.060
When I'm with you, friend...

00:29:42.060 --> 00:29:45.010
hanaretetemo friend...

00:29:42.060 --> 00:29:45.010
When we're apart, friend...
